t statewide run. Fall polling has been unusually close by Vermont standards: a late-September University of New Hampshire survey showed Janoo ahead by six, while other polls gave Scott leads of three to ten points. Outside groups on both sides have launched ad campaigns, and Senator Bernie Sanders' endorsement of Janoo has raised the race's profile.\n\nScott has historically run far ahead of his party in Vermont, winning reelection by wide margins, and polls have tended to underestimate him. Nonpartisan analysts cluster at Likely Republican, and prediction markets give him roughly a three-in-four chance. His incumbency advantage contends with the state's Democratic lean, making this the most competitive Vermont governor's race in years, with Scott still favored.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2101, "margin": -4.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -10.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2344, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2363, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2631, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2569, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1727, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1689, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1678, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1704, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2792, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2255, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1487, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2939, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2369, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2377, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2359, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.1602, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "20